From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:52:42 -0400
Subject: fix: the owner's notes on beta 21, the command-line tabs, issues 9
 and 10, and the round's findings

The owner's twelve notes of 2026-10-20 and the findings that followed, in one
patch because they share the sidebar's views, the tab strip's controller, the
colour supplier and the window's frame (patches/README.md, the round-patch
exception):

- A folder's name is edited only from a double click on the name, in a field
  as wide as the name with the name in it; a double click elsewhere on the
  header only toggles (folders F4). The empty 21 DIP field is gone.
- A top-level folder can join a Space's pinned run, by a drag over the Clear
  line or Pin Folder on its menu (folders F38).
- The rail follows the density: square rows of 44, 36 or 30 DIP, cards as
  wide, gaps that shrink with them (sidebar Y12).
- A tab keeps its site's favicon on a page of the same site that names none
  (tabs R54).
- Closing a pin or an essential, by Cmd-W, its X, a middle click or the menu's
  Close, always unloads it and sends it home, asking first only when the page
  asks before leaving (pins H3, the owner's choice).
- The row's buttons hover and press in the row's own colour (toolbar T43,
  T44); every chip fits the address field (T42); every empty part of the
  window's top is the title bar (sidebar Y29); an extension's popup window
  opens over a full-screen window on the Mac (windows G8).
- Tabs given on the command line load (BACKLOG S-251): the certificate
  verifier service passes a change on only after it has verified a
  certificate, so the first launch's updates no longer drop every connection
  opened ahead of a request.
- A row dragged from the rail onto the page splits it, the rail no longer
  opening under the drag, and a split's panes are named again after a swap
  (splits J10, J11); Ctrl+Alt+Escape during the extension chord is the
  browser's on Windows (toolbar T39); a tab restored asleep draws asleep
  (tabs R46); a rail row shows its hover card (pins H19).
- The review of patches 0075 and 0076: the sleep gate asks about a split the
  model has let go of without a CHECK, and the termination policy asks it
  once a page; the split drop light and the ink centring mirror in
  right-to-left; the split row's icons read on the ground beside a page's
  colour; a replaced pane is watched again.
- Smoother motion (motion O4 to O7): hidden row controls are left out of
  every frame's layout, the sidebar's collapse, expand and overlay ease out,
  and the Space slide's snapshot is a recording the compositor rasters; the
  hidden omnibox popups follow the address field once a motion has ended,
  not at every frame (62 window moves a collapse before).

- The by-hand pass on the release build: a double click renames only what
  both presses hit, and a row the list moves away loses its hover (tabs R1,
  R14); the rail's pause waits while a press is held, so a dragged row stays
  in place over the page (splits J12); a closed pin drops its sound and
  capture marks (pins H24); the tab menu shows each row's shortcut (menus
  M1); the row's buttons, the star and the chips hover at 1.3:1 and press at
  1.6:1 on any page colour (toolbar T44); the chord labels read at 4.5:1 on
  every ground (spaces B18); the rail's pointer watcher reads the event's
  root location, so a row the pointer rests on shows its card (pins H19).
- Spaces switched by a sideways scroll over the sidebar, and on Windows by
  Ctrl with the wheel too (GitHub issue 10, spaces B39, the owner's choice).
- The little window (GitHub issue 9, little E7 to E9): Open in Stedding as a
  button, a page menu row and the File menu's row, Open in Split View beside
  it, Show as Tab doing the same move, and with no normal window one is
  opened; no title bar, the traffic lights inside Stedding's own address row
  in the page's colour.
- Turning vertical tabs back on as a drag ends no longer trips Chromium's
  tab container (BACKLOG S-253).

Tests: each change's new unit and browser tests, each failing with its change
taken out; MotionFramesTest.* measures the frames.

Why: the owner's notes on beta 21, and the round's own checks.
Removable when: never as a whole; the next re-cut gives each part a patch of
its own (patches/README.md).
