 // this lives: a browser test cannot move the real pointer, and a row asks the
 // screen where the pointer is when the row is added to the window. Every other
 // question goes to the real screen, which keeps its displays and observers.
+// Off the Mac the real pointer is held off too: the system's own mouse events
+// are dropped (the switch Chromium's tests set for this,
+// ui::PlatformEventSource::SetIgnoreNativePlatformEvents), and the events
